Prim’s Algorithm
1. Start the program.
2. Read the number of mining sites (vertices) and candidate connections (edges).
3. Represent the mining network using a weighted adjacency matrix.
4. Initialize all vertices as unvisited and set their minimum key values to infinity.
5. Set the key value of the starting vertex to zero.
6. Select the unvisited vertex with the smallest key value.
7. Mark the selected vertex as visited.
8. If the vertex has a parent, display the selected edge and add its weight to the total network cost.
9. Update the key values of adjacent unvisited vertices whenever a lower-cost connection is found.
10. Repeat steps 6–9 until all vertices are visited or no further connection is possible.
11. If all vertices are connected, display the minimum total network cost. Otherwise, report that the network cannot connect all mining sites.
12. Stop the program.
